       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day, and it could cause serious hepatotoxicity. Many institutions cap it at 3 g/day. This patient has normal liver function, but that doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **3000 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also confirm the intended dose with your supervising resident or attending. I can add a note to the order, such as \"max 3 g/day from all sources,\" if you'd like."
