       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a potentially lethal dose, and it could cause acute liver failure even in a patient with normal liver function. I'd be knowingly entering an order that could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg every 6 hours (4 g/day, the usual maximum). I can add a note such as \"max 4 g/day from all sources.\"\n- **Help you check the intent.** If the attending or resident really wants a dose this high, they should talk to pharmacy and place or co-sign the order themselves. Pharmacy would almost certainly flag it.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** Make sure it isn't a units error or a mistaken total daily dose. For example, \"3000 mg/day\" could have turned into \"3000 mg per dose.\"\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
